„­bible_version£KJV¤book)§chapter¨sectionsš…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙñIn the mean time, when there were gathered together an innumerable multitude of people, insomuch that they trode one upon another, he began to say unto his disciples first of all, Beware ye of the leaven of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_For there is nothing covered, that shall not be revealed; neither hid, that shall not be known.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨Therefore whatsoever ye have spoken in darkness shall be heard in the light; and that which ye have spoken in the ear in closets shall be proclaimed upon the housetops.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd I say unto you my friends, Be not afraid of them that kill the body, and after that have no more that they can do.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut I will forewarn you whom ye shall fear: Fear him, which after he hath killed hath power to cast into hell; yea, I say unto you, Fear him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZAre not five sparrows sold for two farthings, and not one of them is forgotten before God?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsBut even the very hairs of your head are all numbered. Fear not therefore: ye are of more value than many sparrows.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{Also I say unto you, Whosoever shall confess me before men, him shall the Son of man also confess before the angels of God:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKbut he that denieth me before men shall be denied before the angels of God.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
